# CODEOWNERS
#
# CODEOWNERS is how per-language adapter maintainers get review rights on the
# directories they own. A team listed here is asked for review on every pull
# request touching its paths, and its members are the maintainers of that
# adapter (see GOVERNANCE.md).
#
# Teams that do not exist yet are placeholders: they are activated when the
# corresponding adapter lands in adapters/<language>/. Until then, the paths
# fall back to the default owner below.
#
# The spec format itself is owned by the initial maintainer and changed only
# through the RFC process (rfcs/).

# Default owner for everything.
* @jbt95

# Core implementation.
src/verispec/ @jbt95

# Conformance corpus: the source of truth for what the spec format supports.
corpus/ @jbt95

# Spec format RFCs.
rfcs/ @jbt95

# Documentation.
docs/ @jbt95

# Per-language adapter maintainers.
adapters/typescript/ @verispec-ts-maintainers
adapters/go/ @verispec-go-maintainers
adapters/rust/ @verispec-rust-maintainers
adapters/c/ @verispec-c-maintainers
adapters/java/ @verispec-java-maintainers
